  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Peel the pumpkin, then cut into 2cm chunks. Cut the tofu into 2cm pieces. Crumble 1 stock cube into a heatproof jug, add 125ml (½ cup) boiling water and stir to dissolve. Stir in the coconut milk.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/129510/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_01-3c5e09c19014ea60abcdf05ac61091d4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brown pumpkin: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Cook the pumpkin and 2 tsp masala seasoning, stirring, for 3-4 mins until golden and fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/129511/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_02-2926580d9bbc8c56d65fa9aea6b809f9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer sauce: Add the coconut stock and season with salt and pepper. Bring to the boil, reduce the heat to medium-low and cook, covered, stirring occasionally, for 12-15 mins until the pumpkin is tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/129512/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_03-a49ec27f5bf99ddf4ba0511d16af9859.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook tofu: Meanwhile, heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium frypan over high heat. Cook the tofu for 2-3 mins each side until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/129513/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_04-bc759d4f4e2c78354fd94ba1a59b85a9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Stir the spinach through the pumpkin curry and cook, uncovered, for a further 1-2 mins until the spinach is wilted. Divide the curry among bowls, top with the tofu and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/129514/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_05-5a7a1690f603c65ff6737795493d279d.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Not counting carbs tonight? Serve with steamed white or brown rice, or some chargrilled naan, on the side. Fry chopped red chillies with the pumpkin if you like a little heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/129515/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_HACK-4d24763fbe97269c0089cc30f420a7fa.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
